s.com/india/now-its-my-turn-sonia-gandhi-predicts-tamasha-as-she-prepares-to-tell-her-own-story/articleshow/135232580.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T17:20:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135233131,imgsize-46776.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The AI social paradox: Better at communicating, worse at connecting?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/the-ai-social-paradox-better-at-communicating-worse-at-connecting/articleshow/135231202.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135231202.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Artificial intelligence increasingly influences our daily conversations, providing quick responses and clarifications. While many appreciate its role in easing social interactions, a growing dependency raises concerns about the erosion of personal communication skills and genuine connections. Moreover, the subtleties and emotions that characterize human interaction could potentially be diminished, raising important debates regarding the implications of AI on our relationships.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/the-ai-social-paradox-better-at-communicating-worse-at-connecting/articleshow/135231202.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/the-ai-social-paradox-better-at-communicating-worse-at-connecting/articleshow/135231202.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T17:10:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135232914,imgsize-265732.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Won't rest till puppet Gyanesh is removed': Cong claims denied permit for mock CEC impeachment; Delhi Police clarifies]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/wont-rest-till-puppet-gyanesh-is-removed-cong-claims-denied-permit-for-mock-cec-impeachment-delhi-police-clarifies/articleshow/135231886.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135231886.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/wont-rest-till-puppet-gyanesh-is-removed-cong-claims-denied-permit-for-mock-cec-impeachment-delhi-police-clarifies/articleshow/135231886.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/wont-rest-till-puppet-gyanesh-is-removed-cong-claims-denied-permit-for-mock-cec-impeachment-delhi-police-clarifies/articleshow/135231886.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T16:35:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135231945,imgsize-93886.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[TOI Youth Icons Summit: CM Yogi highlights UP’s push on jobs, startups and MSMEs, says state now has 25,000 startups]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/toi-youth-icons-summit-cm-yogi-highlights-ups-push-on-jobs-startups-and-msmes-says-state-now-has-25000-startups/articleshow/135231734.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135231734.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Uttar Pradesh chief minister Yogi Adityanath highlighted the state's employment initiatives and youth empowerment at the TOI Youth Icons Summit. He emphasized the growth of the startup ecosystem and initiatives for sports-based employment. The chief minister noted the significant increase in MSME units and direct employment opportunities. Additionally, he mentioned plans for Agniveers and employment for young engineers in defense manufacturing.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/toi-youth-icons-summit-cm-yogi-highlights-ups-push-on-jobs-startups-and-msmes-says-state-now-has-25000-startups/articleshow/135231734.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/toi-youth-icons-summit-cm-yogi-highlights-ups-push-on-jobs-startups-and-msmes-says-state-now-has-25000-startups/articleshow/135231734.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T16:30:08+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135231857,imgsize-37340.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Is Jagan Reddy's 'regret' message a calculated alliance pitch for Congress?]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/is-jagan-reddys-regret-message-a-calculated-alliance-pitch-for-congress/articleshow/135229427.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135229427.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[YSRCP leader YS Jagan Mohan Reddy has publicly acknowledged his mistake of backing the BJP-led NDA government's law to appoint the CEC. Jagan, who was decimated in the 2024 assembly elections, is gearing up to navigate the complicated political landscape as the 2029 elections approach. Speculation abounds regarding a possible alliance with the Congress, creating formidable challenges, especially given the BJP's strong ties with Chandrababu Naidu.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/is-jagan-reddys-regret-message-a-calculated-alliance-pitch-for-congress/articleshow/135229427.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/is-jagan-reddys-regret-message-a-calculated-alliance-pitch-for-congress/articleshow/135229427.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-27T16:25:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kunal Varma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpe